WEBVTT

00:06.139 --> 00:09.710
(Kim Ye Rim)

00:12.579 --> 00:16.116
(Kang Sang Jun)

00:19.419 --> 00:22.923
(Ko Ju Hee, Jung Hyun Min)

00:27.828 --> 00:32.032
(Azure Spring)

00:32.032 --> 00:33.300
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

00:33.300 --> 00:34.535
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

00:34.535 --> 00:35.769
(This drama complied
with production guidelines...)

00:35.769 --> 00:37.004
(for filming child actors and animals.)

02:11.565 --> 02:12.499
Go!

02:12.499 --> 02:13.534
And they're off!

02:13.534 --> 02:16.270
Han Ye Kyung of South Korea
makes a perfectly clean dive.

02:16.770 --> 02:18.071
Now she's breaking the surface.

02:18.071 --> 02:19.773
And she begins her freestyle stroke.

02:20.507 --> 02:22.609
Her strokes are fluid,
and her rhythm is consistent.

02:22.609 --> 02:25.712
She's nearing the halfway mark.

02:26.613 --> 02:28.215
Into the turn!

02:28.916 --> 02:29.883
Looking good!

02:29.883 --> 02:32.019
Perfect touch on the wall,
and a smooth change of direction.

02:32.019 --> 02:34.054
She's picking up the pace with ease.

02:34.321 --> 02:36.990
And now heading into the final ten meters!

02:36.990 --> 02:38.392
Han Ye Kyung.

02:38.392 --> 02:40.627
Han Ye Kyung! Touches!

02:41.628 --> 02:42.529
First place!

02:42.529 --> 02:44.898
It's a gold medal! Gold medal!

02:45.532 --> 02:46.834
What an unbelievable moment!

02:46.834 --> 02:50.170
Gold has returned
to Korean women's swimming.

02:50.537 --> 02:52.873
A rising star and a true dark horse,

02:52.873 --> 02:55.742
Han Ye Kyung finally makes her mark.

02:55.742 --> 02:56.510
Thank you.

02:56.510 --> 02:59.146
What a proud moment for Han Ye Kyung!

02:59.413 --> 03:02.516
We are living in the era of Han Ye Kyung.

03:03.183 --> 03:04.017
(Han Ye Kyung: New National Record
Women's Swimming, South Korea)

03:04.017 --> 03:05.786
Dreams do come true.

03:06.520 --> 03:10.257
(Han Ye Kyung: New National Record
Women's Swimming, South Korea)

03:11.458 --> 03:12.326
Of course,

03:13.327 --> 03:15.195
it doesn't necessarily
have to be my dream.

03:41.154 --> 03:48.128
(Episode 1
Rise or Fall, We're Still Young)

04:33.173 --> 04:34.775
"Pa" for waves, and "Rang" for beauty.

04:35.709 --> 04:37.678
Parang-ri,
where the ripples are beautiful,

04:38.045 --> 04:39.680
even in the mountainous Namhae region,

04:39.680 --> 04:41.415
is a village famous
for its shimmering ripples.

04:44.985 --> 04:46.620
Beyond the edge of Tongyeong,
you have to take a boat...

04:46.620 --> 04:49.523
an hour deeper into the sea
to find this backwater village.

04:54.795 --> 04:55.696
This is...

04:56.563 --> 04:57.664
my hometown.

05:34.067 --> 05:34.968
This is tiring.

06:12.906 --> 06:14.174
It's been five years,

06:14.875 --> 06:16.210
and why is it so spotless?

06:17.644 --> 06:19.146
No need for any cleaning.

08:13.260 --> 08:16.029
Mom never used the iron pot.

08:16.964 --> 08:18.298
After a long day of diving,

08:18.298 --> 08:20.234
hauling over a hundred pounds of seafood,

08:20.767 --> 08:23.103
coming home to this heavy pot...

08:23.504 --> 08:26.840
to lift it, scrub it,
and even grease it down...

08:27.474 --> 08:28.575
was something she refused to do.

08:38.418 --> 08:39.953
But once a year,

08:40.254 --> 08:41.421
on my birthday...

08:41.421 --> 08:43.891
she'd fill this very pot
with the seaweed she'd caught that day...

08:43.891 --> 08:45.292
and cook me seaweed soup.

09:07.514 --> 09:08.649
This is unusual.

09:09.216 --> 09:10.784
At home, for the first time
in a long while,

09:11.585 --> 09:14.521
of all things, I cook seaweed soup
in this iron pot.

09:16.723 --> 09:17.558
Seo Anna.

09:18.125 --> 09:18.992
Happy birthday.

10:04.938 --> 10:06.707
Just living in hiding like this...

10:07.708 --> 10:09.142
might not be that bad.

10:34.434 --> 10:35.435
This is the person!

10:36.537 --> 10:38.138
I told you before, don't you remember?

10:41.508 --> 10:42.809
Good grief.

10:43.210 --> 10:44.745
(Parang Harbor Fishermen's Association)

10:44.745 --> 10:45.579
Where is it?

10:46.346 --> 10:47.181
Here!

10:47.714 --> 10:48.582
Take a look.

10:50.584 --> 10:52.419
- Thanks for the effort.
- Thank you.

10:53.820 --> 10:55.722
There's a kid looking for a room
in the village.

10:55.722 --> 10:57.491
Is it okay to rent out your mom's house?

10:58.926 --> 11:00.327
Just let the person live there.

11:00.327 --> 11:01.695
Having someone in an empty house...

11:01.695 --> 11:02.896
is good for upkeep and all.

11:04.665 --> 11:06.500
(Just let the person live there.)

11:08.769 --> 11:09.603
See?

11:10.938 --> 11:12.306
Anna, are you going to stay long?

11:14.441 --> 11:15.676
Aren't you going to swim anymore?

11:15.676 --> 11:17.110
Who says I'm not? I'm still swimming!

11:17.644 --> 11:19.313
There's no need to snap.

11:20.314 --> 11:21.982
If you're just visiting
for a little while,

11:21.982 --> 11:24.651
then you could stay together like family.

11:25.219 --> 11:26.653
It's not like we're living
in the dark ages.

11:26.987 --> 11:28.589
You've got plenty of rooms,
so what's the big deal?

11:28.589 --> 11:29.489
Chief.

11:30.157 --> 11:32.092
There's no need to be afraid of him.

11:33.293 --> 11:34.695
That was a frost-bound stare.

11:35.629 --> 11:38.165
Anyway, you young folks...

11:38.165 --> 11:41.034
figure this out.

11:41.034 --> 11:41.902
Got it?

11:42.369 --> 11:43.303
Good.

11:43.737 --> 11:44.705
You two look good together.

11:45.772 --> 11:47.841
Something's going to happen for sure.

11:53.914 --> 11:55.115
Now that it's come to this,

11:56.316 --> 11:57.851
let's just make the best of it together.

11:59.386 --> 12:01.788
Tenant in the guest house,
me in the main house.

12:02.322 --> 12:03.991
As long as we don't bother each other.

12:04.324 --> 12:06.226
Even if you hear the phone,
act like you didn't.

12:06.226 --> 12:08.028
Even if you see what I'm eating,
pretend not to see.

12:08.362 --> 12:09.530
Even if we're living under the same roof,

12:09.530 --> 12:10.931
just like living alone, basically.

12:11.498 --> 12:12.599
What do you say, Mr. Tenant?

12:19.106 --> 12:20.307
Well? Nothing to say?

12:21.108 --> 12:23.777
Are you with me on this?

12:23.777 --> 12:24.845
Or are you out?

12:25.312 --> 12:26.547
Will you be staying long?

12:28.182 --> 12:30.184
First the village chief, and now you...

12:30.184 --> 12:32.019
why does everyone keep asking me
how long I'll be here?

12:32.519 --> 12:33.353
Very long...

12:33.654 --> 12:34.888
for a very, very long time.

12:35.322 --> 12:36.223
Forever.

12:36.557 --> 12:37.991
I really hope so.

12:41.662 --> 12:42.863
Did you just blow me off?

12:44.464 --> 12:45.332
Hey.

12:45.832 --> 12:46.700
Hey!

12:51.305 --> 12:52.172
Hey!

12:53.674 --> 12:54.641
Seo Anna!

12:55.375 --> 12:56.510
It's you, right?

12:57.044 --> 12:57.845
Who are you?

12:59.179 --> 13:00.280
It's really you.

13:00.547 --> 13:03.517
The Mermaid of Parang-ri, Seo Anna!

13:04.718 --> 13:06.486
It's been years.

13:06.486 --> 13:07.921
Mermaid, what?

13:09.523 --> 13:11.391
Do you remember me?

13:13.861 --> 13:16.630
The Trot Goddess of Parang-ri.

13:16.630 --> 13:18.265
Baek Su Jeong!

13:18.866 --> 13:22.302
Oh, my goodness
Oh, my goodness, don't do this

13:22.870 --> 13:26.807
A woman's heart is like a reed

13:27.074 --> 13:30.644
Don't do this, what's wrong with you?
Don't ask me

13:31.278 --> 13:35.816
You can't want me anymore

13:36.984 --> 13:40.587
Today it's the first time I met you

13:46.693 --> 13:49.129
Who dares to run away
while the Trot Goddess of Parang-ri...

13:49.129 --> 13:50.531
is performing?

13:50.764 --> 13:51.798
Sorry.

13:52.633 --> 13:54.801
I've got swimming practice.

13:55.736 --> 13:57.838
Fair enough, the Little Mermaid
needs her swim training.

13:58.238 --> 13:59.873
Have a great time! Keep it up!

14:00.374 --> 14:01.375
Okay, got it.

14:03.343 --> 14:04.311
Now, focus.

14:04.311 --> 14:05.245
I'll start over.

14:06.079 --> 14:09.650
Oh, my goodness
Oh, my goodness, don't do this

14:13.587 --> 14:14.688
I'm doomed.

14:17.257 --> 14:18.859
So much for living on my own.

14:19.626 --> 14:22.196
Truly, a singer's voice
is their fingerprint.

14:22.496 --> 14:24.865
I guess you remembered me
as soon as you heard the song?

14:26.066 --> 14:26.934
I knew it.

14:27.734 --> 14:29.603
And so much for living a quiet life.

14:30.070 --> 14:31.004
And so,

14:31.305 --> 14:33.040
I heard you went to Seoul
to be a competitive swimmer.

14:33.307 --> 14:34.541
Why are you back out of the blue?

14:37.544 --> 14:38.412
Well...

14:38.912 --> 14:40.681
The Parang-ri Mermaid,
who was said to be a swimmer in Seoul,

14:41.014 --> 14:42.683
is actually...

14:53.160 --> 14:54.328
My goodness...

14:54.695 --> 14:56.597
you look tired these days.

14:57.097 --> 14:59.533
Your boyfriend must be quite strong?

15:01.368 --> 15:02.269
What?

15:02.269 --> 15:04.771
I said, your boyfriend
must be quite strong.

15:04.771 --> 15:05.672
Tidy up here.

15:09.843 --> 15:11.411
Little Mermaid? Yeah, right.

15:13.547 --> 15:16.717
I'm no longer the Parang-ri Mermaid.

15:22.422 --> 15:24.124
Hey, stop. Stay still.

15:24.124 --> 15:24.992
Don't move.

15:25.359 --> 15:26.560
Hey, don't move.

15:27.361 --> 15:28.896
Today, your...

15:30.330 --> 15:32.299
your booty is in top shape.

15:32.900 --> 15:36.003
One little brush against this,

15:36.370 --> 15:37.905
it feels like it's about to snap.

15:38.972 --> 15:39.873
Hey!

15:42.843 --> 15:45.012
Hey. Did you just say "hey" to me?

15:45.279 --> 15:46.146
You heard me. I said "hey."

15:46.146 --> 15:47.915
What! You creep!

15:47.915 --> 15:50.184
- I'm going to kill you!
- Watch your language with me.

15:50.884 --> 15:53.387
You're lucky I'm letting this slide today.

15:54.154 --> 15:56.089
- You are so dead.
- Wait.

15:57.291 --> 15:58.458
Hey, my nose is bleeding.

16:00.294 --> 16:01.628
Hey, Seo Anna.

16:02.095 --> 16:04.298
Don't bother coming in from tomorrow!

16:06.266 --> 16:07.835
You're fired!

16:26.086 --> 16:27.821
It's been a while
since I've actually swum.

16:28.889 --> 16:30.757
I just worked a part-time job at a pool,
but I lost it.

16:34.228 --> 16:36.697
There's no need to
tell this to Parang-ri's...

16:37.297 --> 16:38.899
chatterbox, Baek Su Jeong.

16:40.334 --> 16:41.335
Why are you back?

16:42.669 --> 16:45.205
I mean, why are you here?

16:45.973 --> 16:46.840
Just.

16:48.108 --> 16:49.176
It's just so unfair.

16:49.176 --> 16:50.010
Unfair?

16:50.777 --> 16:51.612
What is?

16:52.913 --> 16:53.881
By the way,

16:54.448 --> 16:56.483
about the guy who lives in my house.

16:57.150 --> 16:58.418
Are you talking about Deok Hyun?

16:59.720 --> 17:00.587
He's older?

17:01.421 --> 17:02.456
Anyway.

17:02.456 --> 17:04.558
What's his deal?

17:06.226 --> 17:07.327
A male sea diver.

17:07.594 --> 17:08.996
- A male diver?
- Yes.

17:09.296 --> 17:10.697
He dives for a living.

17:10.964 --> 17:11.965
And he looks...

17:13.267 --> 17:15.035
incredibly cool doing it.

17:28.115 --> 17:30.317
Deok Hyun, nice!

17:33.320 --> 17:36.557
Though the area is a bit uphill,

17:36.790 --> 17:38.759
you'll be okay after a few trips.

17:39.793 --> 17:40.861
Nice.

17:40.861 --> 17:42.029
Ain't it nice?

17:44.631 --> 17:45.465
This place...

17:47.100 --> 17:48.735
has an incredible view.

17:49.770 --> 17:51.104
His name is Yun Deok Hyun.

17:51.338 --> 17:53.006
Age, occupation, and past...

17:53.941 --> 17:55.075
unknown.

17:55.075 --> 17:57.711
Out of nowhere one day...

17:58.979 --> 18:01.882
Drifted in like the wind

18:01.882 --> 18:03.784
A mysterious young man

18:05.686 --> 18:06.520
Wait.

18:07.287 --> 18:08.255
No way...

18:09.389 --> 18:11.058
are you interested in Deok Hyun too?

18:11.525 --> 18:12.426
Too?

18:15.395 --> 18:17.764
Don't tell me you're interested in him.

18:19.800 --> 18:21.001
You tell me first.

18:21.268 --> 18:22.903
Weren't you only staying for a short bit?

18:22.903 --> 18:24.304
Aren't you going to swim?

18:24.304 --> 18:26.240
I am. I'm going to.

18:26.406 --> 18:27.908
Why are you being like this too?

18:28.609 --> 18:30.777
Plus, I'm not interested in him at all.

18:32.212 --> 18:33.747
What's there to like about such a jerk?

18:34.448 --> 18:36.283
A jerk?

18:37.050 --> 18:39.486
A young male diver shrouded in mystery.

18:40.521 --> 18:42.356
Isn't that too sexy?

18:44.558 --> 18:45.526
Sexy?

19:11.351 --> 19:13.353
What part of him is even remotely sexy?

19:13.353 --> 19:14.788
He's just dark and tanned, that's all.

19:18.725 --> 19:20.194
Oh, you got a baby sea bream there?

19:20.194 --> 19:21.795
That'll be so tasty in a soup.

19:21.995 --> 19:23.197
Didn't we agree...

19:23.197 --> 19:25.365
to just look the other way
regarding what we eat?

19:28.535 --> 19:30.704
I'm just saying, that's all.

19:31.805 --> 19:34.274
Like I said, baby sea bream
is really good in soup.

19:35.209 --> 19:36.143
Information!

19:46.019 --> 19:47.120
Sexy? Sure.

19:47.921 --> 19:49.356
He's a snotty scumbag.

19:51.525 --> 19:53.060
What the...

20:18.051 --> 20:19.553
This middle-of-nowhere village.

20:20.254 --> 20:22.122
Eating is the only joy.

20:25.559 --> 20:26.593
Wake up, Seo Anna.

20:27.361 --> 20:28.929
Like he'd actually give it to me
if I asked.

20:29.229 --> 20:30.497
Have you no pride?

21:07.034 --> 21:08.735
(Snack Bar
Sea Squirt & Pork Belly Available)

21:08.735 --> 21:10.370
(Ramyeon, Gimbap, Noodles)

21:14.775 --> 21:16.376
What kind of snack bar closes at seven?

21:29.857 --> 21:30.958
Why aren't you answering my calls?

21:31.291 --> 21:32.626
Don't tell me you blocked me?

21:33.694 --> 21:36.196
Are you unaware of how tight
the owner is with the association?

21:37.431 --> 21:39.399
Are you going to quit swimming for good?

21:39.399 --> 21:40.234
(Ignore xxx)

21:50.077 --> 21:51.578
Where did all that sparkle go?

21:52.946 --> 21:54.281
It's just pitch black now.

21:55.549 --> 21:58.418
It's so dark,
even a ghost could hide.

22:21.074 --> 22:22.009
I'm hungry.

22:42.930 --> 22:43.997
Mr. Tenant!

22:45.933 --> 22:46.867
Anybody there?

22:51.705 --> 22:52.573
Is he gone?

22:54.308 --> 22:55.609
Excuse me.

23:01.014 --> 23:02.115
You out?

23:10.324 --> 23:11.692
Wow, so organized.

23:12.526 --> 23:13.794
Typical. This says everything about him.

23:21.602 --> 23:23.403
Where did he hide it?

23:34.214 --> 23:36.917
Never lose that food radar, Seo Anna.

23:48.161 --> 23:49.096
Sea squirts?

23:49.863 --> 23:51.498
Why did he freeze these beauties?

23:51.932 --> 23:53.834
Should've mixed in a bowl of rice
right then and there.

23:56.203 --> 23:57.371
Well, I guess I'll have to
eat them myself.

24:00.174 --> 24:02.776
(Parang-ri)

24:02.776 --> 24:04.578
Chief, I'd like to use the field a bit.

24:04.578 --> 24:05.812
Do as you please.

25:01.602 --> 25:03.270
Nothing soothes you in the morning...

25:03.270 --> 25:05.973
like a bowl of clear fish soup.

25:08.909 --> 25:11.845
If you make that clear fish soup
with pufferfish, it's pufferfish soup.

25:12.246 --> 25:14.515
And if you use a baby sea bream,
like me right now...

25:14.915 --> 25:16.350
then it becomes baby sea bream soup.

25:50.484 --> 25:53.387
The classic way for sea squirt
is mixing it on the spot with rice,

25:53.387 --> 25:55.589
lettuce, and a dash of sesame oil.

25:56.890 --> 25:58.525
Still, sea squirts
that missed their timing...

25:59.092 --> 26:01.728
can be a real treat
when made into pancakes.

26:18.846 --> 26:21.148
When ingredients are iffy,

26:21.148 --> 26:22.449
Rule one of solo living...

26:26.253 --> 26:27.221
oil is the answer.

27:35.522 --> 27:36.423
I should...

27:37.858 --> 27:38.926
go back, right?

27:49.136 --> 27:51.371
Does sharing the kitchen
include sharing the food too?

27:52.372 --> 27:53.307
Gosh, you scared me.

27:57.444 --> 27:58.378
Well, you see...

27:58.912 --> 28:00.147
I thought you'd thrown them away.

28:01.181 --> 28:03.483
Then, they'd be in the trash,

28:03.483 --> 28:04.551
not the freezer.

28:06.787 --> 28:09.690
It's just fish scraps and sea squirt.
Don't be so cheap about it.

28:10.123 --> 28:11.792
Do you think catching sea squirts is easy?

28:12.793 --> 28:14.528
Don't act so special
just because you dive.

28:15.629 --> 28:17.965
I was quite a swimmer myself, you know.

28:18.232 --> 28:19.733
You're using the past tense,

28:19.733 --> 28:21.034
so I guess you no longer...

28:23.437 --> 28:24.271
swim.

28:25.906 --> 28:27.341
- What?
- Or...

28:28.108 --> 28:29.109
you can't.

28:30.844 --> 28:32.713
Hey, what do you know about me?

28:32.713 --> 28:34.948
Whatever it is, it'll be best
to make up your mind soon.

28:35.249 --> 28:36.149
About what?

28:37.518 --> 28:39.686
Whether you're going to commit
and settle down here.

28:39.686 --> 28:41.054
Or if you're just here for a breather...

28:41.054 --> 28:42.389
before going back to your old life.

28:43.524 --> 28:45.792
People who wallow in self-pity,

28:45.792 --> 28:47.561
ruin this village's mood,
and then just leave.

28:47.995 --> 28:49.062
I've seen it all too many times.

28:52.299 --> 28:53.200
Information.

29:03.610 --> 29:04.578
Seo Anna!

29:08.248 --> 29:09.616
Why'd you quit your part-time job?

29:10.050 --> 29:11.952
Don't you know who the boss is?

29:13.520 --> 29:14.688
How could I not know.

29:15.355 --> 29:17.291
Yes, I was obsessed because
I never got Mom that gold medal,

29:17.291 --> 29:19.092
and so I trained
day and night without rest.

29:19.092 --> 29:21.195
So you pulled strings to get this job...

29:21.562 --> 29:23.764
for your "washed-up" girlfriend.

29:24.331 --> 29:26.099
You said he's close
with the association president...

29:26.099 --> 29:28.235
and that he could help my comeback
even after a few years off.

29:28.235 --> 29:29.303
You know exactly!

29:30.337 --> 29:31.738
But you screw up like that?

29:33.507 --> 29:35.275
Do you really want to ruin your life?

29:36.476 --> 29:37.978
How can everyone so easily judge...

29:39.413 --> 29:41.782
whether someone's life is ruined or not?

29:43.684 --> 29:45.452
As your swim coach for nine years.

29:46.253 --> 29:47.855
As your boyfriend for three years.

29:49.389 --> 29:51.758
Anna, I've known you for 12 years.

29:52.993 --> 29:53.827
Right?

29:55.762 --> 29:57.197
Are you done with swimming?

29:57.998 --> 30:00.968
Do you want your name
to stay as Seo Anna, the failed prospect?

30:10.744 --> 30:11.645
Seo Anna.

30:12.813 --> 30:13.914
This is my last warning.

30:15.215 --> 30:16.183
Put down the suitcase.

30:18.352 --> 30:19.453
Jerks.

30:20.287 --> 30:21.255
You're going to pay for this.

30:27.361 --> 30:28.495
Where did he go?

31:26.353 --> 31:27.621
Since when was there a sea like this...

31:29.489 --> 31:30.824
hidden behind Parang-ri?

31:37.264 --> 31:38.031
What?

31:38.432 --> 31:39.199
What's that!

32:40.527 --> 32:41.929
Rise or fall, we're still young.

32:43.197 --> 32:45.599
Thank you.

32:45.866 --> 32:47.067
Silence.

32:47.601 --> 32:48.569
Enough eating.

32:48.569 --> 32:49.503
Everyone focus.

32:50.003 --> 32:51.705
Our Korea National Sport University.

32:52.506 --> 32:53.473
Our ace,

32:54.141 --> 32:55.475
Ye Kyung will give a toast.

32:56.977 --> 32:58.178
Our ace.

32:58.579 --> 33:02.482
Ace!

33:03.116 --> 33:04.117
I'll go with...

33:05.319 --> 33:07.321
"Rise or fall, we're still young!"

33:07.955 --> 33:09.122
Rise or fall!

33:09.122 --> 33:11.391
We're still young!

33:13.827 --> 33:15.462
- Bottoms up.
- Okay.

33:16.096 --> 33:17.030
Eat up.

33:17.030 --> 33:18.532
Even this isn't enough.

33:27.274 --> 33:30.310
They say, "Rise or fall,
we're still young."

33:34.915 --> 33:38.218
But the youth I knew wasn't like that.

33:54.668 --> 33:55.903
Success is youth,

34:00.307 --> 34:03.510
but failure is just pathetic.

34:14.755 --> 34:17.891
That's why I hate being called a failure.

34:18.959 --> 34:20.394
I fought just as hard as anyone else.

34:21.695 --> 34:22.596
No,

34:23.063 --> 34:24.765
maybe I fought even harder than they did.

34:44.284 --> 34:45.185
What is it?

34:45.953 --> 34:47.020
How did you find this place?

34:53.293 --> 34:54.494
Teach me how to dive too.

34:58.432 --> 34:59.299
What?

34:59.766 --> 35:01.702
Let's just say the fish heads were trash,

35:02.169 --> 35:04.238
but I'll make up for the sea squirts.
I'll dive for them.

35:06.740 --> 35:08.208
It was just a passing remark.

35:08.575 --> 35:09.443
Forget about it.

35:11.111 --> 35:11.979
Hey!

35:15.782 --> 35:18.685
Who blabs about someone's life
being ruined as a passing remark?

35:19.720 --> 35:20.854
I'm a good swimmer.

35:21.388 --> 35:24.057
I was even a national youth athlete.

35:24.992 --> 35:27.060
If you show me how,

35:28.495 --> 35:29.930
I'll get those sea squirts for you.

35:31.765 --> 35:32.866
So,

35:34.535 --> 35:35.802
teach me how...

35:36.837 --> 35:37.804
to dive.

35:41.975 --> 35:43.143
My life isn't ruined.

35:45.012 --> 35:46.246
Parang-ri Mermaid...

35:46.780 --> 35:48.081
isn't washed up yet.

35:58.959 --> 35:59.826
(Mi Hyun's daughter)

35:59.826 --> 36:01.295
Just let the person live there.

36:03.030 --> 36:04.131
She says just live here.

36:05.999 --> 36:06.867
Okay.

36:07.267 --> 36:08.669
But I'll still pay the rent.

36:10.504 --> 36:12.206
Make yourself at home.

36:13.607 --> 36:16.543
You can use a room in the main house
or the guest house.

36:37.764 --> 36:39.399
She looks like a real handful.

37:41.228 --> 37:43.230
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
